module Core

### Marker protocol for the access-synchronization discipline of a {Shared[T, P]}.
###
### A policy carries the lock STATE (if any) and provides the acquire/release primitives that
### `Shared.inspect()` / `Shared.claim!()` drive. The discipline ALSO determines, at compile time,
### which access tokens are legal — `ReadOnly` grants only `Inspecting`, `Exclusive` only `Claiming`,
### `MultiRead` both — enforced statically by the readers-XOR-writer borrow checker.
###
### `P` is a type parameter of `Shared`/`ShareController`, so each discipline is selected by
### monomorphization (no runtime dispatch): the controller's `lock` field is laid out per `P`
### (`ReadOnly` is zero-sized → no overhead) and the acquire/release calls are statically inlined.
### :see: {ReadOnly}, {Exclusive}, {MultiRead}, {Shared}
protocol LockPolicy
  pass
